# =====================================================================================
# monoid_identity.rq — RED->GREEN probe for T-MONOID (the two-sided identity tooth,
# W2 · SP0). Re-homes algebra_spine.ttl q_monoid_identity / fnd:MonoidIdentityShape
# (:631-653) into the folded stratified idiom, over the unified @rel:* reified-table
# vocabulary (bridges.ttl:249-291: relation:structure = fnd:opStructure,
# relation:category:first/second/result = fnd:opLeft/opRight/opResult).
# =====================================================================================
# The MONOID two-sided identity law: for every model carrying an identity element e
# (@rel:identity:element e), no reified composition row (a Cayley-table cell scoped to
# the model by @rel:structure) with e as its FIRST operand may yield a result != its
# SECOND operand (left-unit e·x = x), and no row with e as its SECOND operand may yield
# a result != its FIRST operand (right-unit x·e = x). This SELECT returns every row that
# VIOLATES that — the model, the offending cell, the two operands and the wrong result.
#
#   GREEN (a genuine monoid, e.g. fixtures/monoid_z2.ttl — Z/2 under + with e=0):
#         0 rows — every identity row yields the other operand, the tooth is satisfied.
#   RED   (a broken monoid, e.g. fixtures/monoid_z2_negative.ttl — the row e·1 yields e
#         instead of 1): >= 1 row — the left-unit law fails and the tooth bites.
#
# Run over the algebra data graph merged with the fixture under test, inference=none.
# Companion SHACL tooth: shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl MonoidModelIdentityShape (sh:sparql,
# sh:targetClass rec:model:record) flips conforms True->False under the same injection.
# The complementary "monoid = one-object category" seam (algebra_spine.ttl:445
# q_monoid_is_endo / fnd:MonoidIsEndoShape / fnd:endoMonoidWitness) is a Pillar-4 category
# seam OUTSIDE the one-operation spine and is EXPLICITLY DEFERRED to the category fan-out
# (design §7.4) — it is NOT dropped, it re-homes there.

PREFIX rel: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:>

SELECT ?model ?cell ?first ?second ?result WHERE {
  ?model rel:identity:element ?e .
  ?cell  rel:structure        ?model ;
         rel:category:first   ?first ;
         rel:category:second  ?second ;
         rel:category:result  ?result .
  FILTER(
       ( ?first  = ?e && ?result != ?second )   # left-unit  e·x = x  violated
    || ( ?second = ?e && ?result != ?first  )   # right-unit x·e = x  violated
  )
}
